# Cursor AI Rules for LUDUS Platform

## Project Overview
This is the LUDUS social activity platform - a comprehensive full-stack application built with React frontend and Node.js backend, deployed on Render.

## MCP (Model Context Protocol) Integration
The project includes a comprehensive MCP server for Render API integration that allows AI agents to:
- List and manage Render services
- Trigger deployments
- Monitor service logs and metrics
- Update environment variables
- Get deployment history

## Available MCP Tools
- `list_render_services`: List all Render services
- `get_service_status`: Get status of a specific service
- `deploy_service`: Trigger manual deployment
- `get_service_logs`: Retrieve service logs
- `get_service_metrics`: Get performance metrics
- `update_service_env`: Update environment variables

## MCP Server Location
- Main server: `scripts/render-mcp-server.js`
- API routes: `server/src/routes/renderMCP.js`
- Controller: `server/src/controllers/renderMCPController.js`

## Development Guidelines
1. Always use the MCP tools when working with Render services
2. Test MCP functionality before deploying changes
3. Use proper authentication when calling MCP endpoints
4. Follow the established error handling patterns

## Key Files
- MCP Server: `scripts/render-mcp-server.js`
- MCP Routes: `server/src/routes/renderMCP.js`
- MCP Controller: `server/src/controllers/renderMCPController.js`
- Test Scripts: `test-render-mcp.js`
- Documentation: `docs_archive/RENDER_MCP_INTEGRATION_GUIDE.md`
